Backport of https://github.com/bazelbuild/rules_swift/pull/1535
("Remove prints when toolchain is skipped"), which landed upstream after
2.5.0 and first shipped in rules_swift 3.0.0.

rules_swift is a transitive dependency of flatbuffers, grpc and rules_apple.
Envoy builds no Swift on Linux, so the autoconfiguration repo rule finds no
'swiftc' and printed a DEBUG message on every single build. The 3.x line is
not a drop-in replacement (compatibility_level 2 -> 3), so the fix is
backported onto 2.5.0 here instead.
===================================================================
--- a/swift/internal/swift_autoconfiguration.bzl
+++ b/swift/internal/swift_autoconfiguration.bzl
@@ -208,10 +208,6 @@
     """
     path_to_swiftc = repository_ctx.which("swiftc")
     if not path_to_swiftc:
-        print("""\
-No 'swiftc' executable found in $PATH. Not auto-generating a Linux Swift \
-toolchain.
-""")  # buildifier: disable=print
         repository_ctx.file(
             "BUILD",
             """\
@@ -352,10 +348,6 @@
 def _create_windows_toolchain(repository_ctx):
     path_to_swiftc = repository_ctx.which("swiftc.exe")
     if not path_to_swiftc:
